  "what": "Every published vintage of the daily series, as an exact reconstruction recipe: truncate the current history.csv at the vintage's last_observation, then overwrite the values in its diffs. Gives a backtester the numbers as they stood on any publish date -- the ALFRED property -- without twelve git invocations.",
  "reconstruction": "rows = {d: r for d, r in current.items() if d <= last_observation and d not in absent_days}; then for each diff day, apply its channel values over the row. Verified exact against git for every vintage listed, on every build; the builder refuses to publish otherwise.",
  "why_diffs": "10 of the vintages differ from today's series by nothing at all (vintages.json is the nightly proof), so a full panel would be >99% duplication. The two revised vintages carry their changed values inline.",
